4. How do new documents enter the AI knowledge base?
This is what makes it a real company solution rather than a demo.

Imagine an employee uploads a new deployment manual to SharePoint.

You create an automated ingestion workflow:


New document uploaded


Retool Workflow triggered


Extract document text


Split into chunks


Generate embeddings


Update PostgreSQL + pgvector


You also need to handle document updates and deletions so employees don't receive outdated instructions.

For a production system, consider:
- Document versioning.
- Department-level access control.
- Document expiration.
- Source permissions inherited from SharePoint or Confluence.
- Re-indexing when documents change.
Very important: Don't rely only on the AI agent's instructions for security. The retrieval tool itself must enforce employee permissions before returning document content.
